<+>{\r\n \"cells\": [\r\n  {\r\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\r\n   \"id\": \"5bc9be56\",\r\n   \"metadata\": {},\r\n   \"source\": [\r\n    \"## Sentiment Analysis\"\r\n   ]\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\r\n   \"id\": \"818b3b52\",\r\n   \"metadata\": {},\r\n   \"source\": [\r\n    \"In this exercise we use the IMDb-dataset, which we will use to perform a sentiment analysis. The code below assumes that the data is placed in the same folder as this notebook. We see that the reviews are loaded as a pandas dataframe, and print the beginning of the first few reviews.\"\r\n   ]\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"metadata\": {\r\n    \"ExecuteTime\": {\r\n     \"end_time\": \"2025-04-08T08:12:27.104364Z\",\r\n     \"start_time\": \"2025-04-08T08:12:27.097614Z\"\r\n    }\r\n   },\r\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\r\n   \"source\": [\r\n    \"import numpy as np\\n\",\r\n    \"import pandas as pd\\n\",\r\n    \"from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\\n\",\r\n    \"from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import CountVectorizer\\n\",\r\n    \"from sklearn.neural_network import MLPClassifier\\n\",\r\n    \"from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, classification_report, confusion_matrix\"\r\n   ],\r\n   \"id\": \"af6c58300999ffc5\",\r\n   \"outputs\": [],\r\n   \"execution_count\": 8\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\r\n   \"id\": \"67da3bc0\",\r\n   \"metadata\": {\r\n    \"ExecuteTime\": {\r\n     \"end_time\": \"2025-04-08T07:20:27.941351Z\",\r\n     \"start_time\": \"2025-04-08T07:20:27.523432Z\"\r\n    }\r\n   },\r\n   \"source\": [\r\n    \"reviews = pd.read_csv('reviews.txt', header=None)\\n\",\r\n    \"labels = pd.read_csv('labels.txt', header=None)\\n\",\r\n    \"Y = (labels=='positive').astype(np.int_)\\n\",\r\n    \"\\n\",\r\n    \"print(type(reviews))\\n\",\r\n    \"print(reviews.head())\"\r\n   ],\r\n   \"outputs\": [\r\n    {\r\n     \"name\": \"stdout\",\r\n     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\r\n     \"text\": [\r\n      \"<class 'pandas.core.frame.DataFrame'>\\n\",\r\n      \"                                                   0\\n\",\r\n      \"0  bromwell high is a cartoon comedy . it ran at ...\\n\",\r\n      \"1  story of a man who has unnatural feelings for ...\\n\",\r\n      \"2  homelessness  or houselessness as george carli...\\n\",\r\n      \"3  airport    starts as a brand new luxury    pla...\\n\",\r\n      \"4  brilliant over  acting by lesley ann warren . ...\\n\"\r\n     ]\r\n    }\r\n   ],\r\n   \"execution_count\": 3\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\r\n   \"id\": \"4982b946\",\r\n   \"metadata\": {},\r\n   \"source\": [\r\n    \"**(a)** Split the reviews and labels in test, train and validation sets. The train and validation sets will be used to train your model and tune hyperparameters, the test set will be saved for testing. Use the `CountVectorizer` from `sklearn.feature_extraction.text` to create a Bag-of-Words representation of the reviews. Only use the 10,000 most frequent words (use the `max_features`-parameter of `CountVectorizer`).\"\r\n   ]\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"metadata\": {\r\n    \"ExecuteTime\": {\r\n     \"end_time\": \"2025-04-08T07:20:33.125033Z\",\r\n     \"start_time\": \"2025-04-08T07:20:28.280552Z\"\r\n    }\r\n   },\r\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\r\n   \"source\": [\r\n    \"# Flatten Y to a 1D array\\n\",\r\n    \"Y = Y.values.ravel()\\n\",\r\n    \"\\n\",\r\n    \"# Split the data: 60% train, 20% validation, 20% test\\n\",\r\n    \"X_train_val, X_test, y_train_val, y_test = train_test_split(reviews[0], Y, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\\n\",\r\n    \"X_train, X_val, y_train, y_val = train_test_split(X_train_val, y_train_val, test_size=0.25, random_state=42)  # 0.25 * 0.8 = 0.2\\n\",\r\n    \"\\n\",\r\n    \"# Initialize CountVectorizer with max 10,000 features\\n\",\r\n    \"vectorizer = CountVectorizer(max_features=10000)\\n\",\r\n    \"\\n\",\r\n    \"# Fit and transform the training data; transform the validation and test data\\n\",\r\n    \"X_train_bow = vectorizer.fit_transform(X_train)\\n\",\r\n    \"X_val_bow = vectorizer.transform(X_val)\\n\",\r\n    \"X_test_bow = vectorizer.transform(X_test)\\n\",\r\n    \"\\n\",\r\n    \"# Optional: Print shape of datasets\\n\",\r\n    \"print(f\\\"Train set shape: {X_train_bow.shape}\\\")\\n\",\r\n    \"print(f\\\"Validation set shape: {X_val_bow.shape}\\\")\\n\",\r\n    \"print(f\\\"Test set shape: {X_test_bow.shape}\\\")\"\r\n   ],\r\n   \"id\": \"c5957748965a5eab\",\r\n   \"outputs\": [\r\n    {\r\n     \"name\": \"stdout\",\r\n     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\r\n     \"text\": [\r\n      \"Train set shape: (15000, 10000)\\n\",\r\n      \"Validation set shape: (5000, 10000)\\n\",\r\n      \"Test set shape: (5000, 10000)\\n\"\r\n     ]\r\n    }\r\n   ],\r\n   \"execution_count\": 4\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\r\n   \"id\": \"ebf07ee9\",\r\n   \"metadata\": {},\r\n   \"source\": [\r\n    \"**(b)** Explore the representation of the reviews. How is a single word represented? How about a whole review?\"\r\n   ]\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n   \"metadata\": {\r\n    \"ExecuteTime\": {\r\n     \"end_time\": \"2025-04-08T07:23:55.648275Z\",\r\n     \"start_time\": \"2025-04-08T07:23:54.583758Z\"\r\n    }\r\n   },\r\n   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\r\n   \"source\": [\r\n    \"# Each column in the Bag-of-Words matrix corresponds to a word.\\n\",\r\n    \"# Get the first 10 words from the vectorizer's vocabulary\\n\",\r\n    \"print(\\\"First 10 words in the vocabulary:\\\")\\n\",\r\n    \"print(vectorizer.get_feature_names_out()[:10])\\n\",\r\n    \"\\n\",\r\n    \"# Let's inspect one review from the training set\\n\",\r\n    \"review_example = X_train.iloc[0]\\n\",\r\n    \"print(\\\"\\\\nOriginal review text:\\\")\\n\",\r\n    \"print(review_example)\\n\",\r\n    \"\\n\",\r\n    \"# Convert this review to its Bag-of-Words representation (sparse vector)\\n\",\r\n    \"review_vector = vectorizer.transform([review_example])\\n\",\r\n    \"print(\\\"\